VERDICT: NULL. Division-by-frustration (try_divide, division.py:81) accepts a
split only when a feature dim is BIMODAL across samples (both children cohere
> NULL_SPLIT=0.72; a uniform dim splits to 2/pi=0.64 and is rejected). RFF's
dense random projection sin(2pi*W*r+b) mixes all inputs into every output dim,
so each dim is smooth-unimodal (low bw) or uniform-noise (high bw) -- never
cleanly bimodal -> no dim passes the split test -> class discovery never fires
-> organism collapses to 1 class. Robust across bandwidth. The feature space is
fine; it is structurally incompatible with frustration-division class discovery.
Contrast: Gabor energy has per-dim on/off structure -> division OVER-fires (128).
Both are failure modes of the same division machinery (the s038 keystone).
